	quest.544D301000110001.title: "Choose Your Magic Controls"
	quest.544D301000110001.quest_desc: ["Too Much Magic keeps Minecraft's normal movement, combat, and inventory controls. For a fresh player, mod-added keybindings are intended to start unbound so dozens of mods cannot silently fight over shortcuts. Open Options > Controls > Key Binds to assign only the magic and utility actions you want. Controlling helps find bindings and conflicts. Your changes are personal; this quest does not reset anything. KeySets is included for one test build and may be removed if its controls or saved profiles prove unreliable."]
	task.544D4D1200000001.title: "Any Log or Stem"
	quest.544D309000100001.title: "I'm Ready for Regular Mode"
	quest.544D309000100001.quest_desc: ["New players begin in Newbie Mode, with protected inventory/experience and convenience travel, but without MXP or faction enrollment. When YOU are ready for full survival progression, check this box and claim your personal graduation reward. This permanently enables Regular Mode for your character: normal death and Corail graves, no home/rtp/back, MXP and class enrollment. Graduation is one-way without an administrator. In a team, each player must claim their own reward; never force graduation on teammates."]
	quest.544DB10000000001.title: "The Monk Path"
	quest.544DB10000000001.quest_desc: ["Monks cultivate unarmed combat, movement and survival through class trials. Consult the Monk path in the skill interface and follow its current initiation requirements; the intended sunset initiation and reserved fist slot are subject to the integrated path data. Claiming this guide does not enroll you."]
	quest.544DB10000000002.title: "The Hunter Path"
	quest.544DB10000000002.quest_desc: ["Hunters specialize against creature families and gain progression through qualifying kills. The intended initiation uses poison while regeneration is active; follow the current path requirements and then choose a specialization. Mutagenic Brews and permanent mutations are separate progression milestones; verify implemented recipes and effects in JEI. This guide does not enroll you."]
	quest.544DB10000000003.title: "The Gilded Path"
	quest.544DB10000000003.quest_desc: ["Gilded is a planned TMM character path using the shared Progression engine. Inspect the available path definitions in your build. If no Gilded enrollment or tree is exposed, it is not yet available; this guide does not imply any implemented requirements or powers."]
	quest.544DB10000000004.title: "Becoming a Vampire"
	quest.544DB10000000004.quest_desc: ["JAWR owns vampirism in this pack; the separate Vampirism mod is retired. Consult JAWR's in-game guide for the native transformation and Lilith's blood route; inspect the Vampire skill category after successful transformation. Blood feeding and sunlight are native mechanics. This checkmark does not change your form."]
	quest.544DB10000000005.title: "Becoming a Werewolf"
	quest.544DB10000000005.quest_desc: ["JAWR also owns lycanthropy; the separate Werewolves mod is retired. Consult the JAWR in-game guide and its wolfsbane-related transformation route, then inspect the Werewolf skill category. Follow the current native cure rules before changing forms. This checkmark is not a transformation trigger."]
	quest.544DB10000000006.title: "Becoming a Dragon"
	quest.544DB10000000006.quest_desc: ["Dragon Survival provides Cave, Forest and Sea dragon forms with different diets and abilities. Open its native species selection interface when installed and eligible; consult the current controls and diet tooltips before choosing. TMM's diet and form compatibility are subject to live testing. This quest is an informational guide, not a species setter."]
	quest.544DB10000000007.title: "Lichdom: Forbidden Magic"
	quest.544DB10000000007.quest_desc: ["JAWR: Forbidden Magic provides its own lich path and phylactery. Use the mod's guide for the native ritual, soul storage, resurrection anchor and cure; check the corresponding Tyz category after transformation where implemented. This guide does not grant lichdom or create a resurrection anchor."]
	quest.544DB10000000008.title: "Lichdom: Goety"
	quest.544DB10000000008.quest_desc: ["Goety offers a distinct lich path. Follow the native guide's lich ritual and prepare the Arca for native soul storage and resurrection. The Goety chapter owns its general ritual and summoning progression; character form guidance lives here. No transformation is granted by this quest."]
	quest.544DB10000000009.title: "The Archlich"
	quest.544DB10000000009.quest_desc: ["The intended Archlich combines the two distinct lich paths, with JAWR phylactery-first resurrection and Goety Arca fallback. This compatibility is experimental; do not treat it as a third independent lich source or assume untested death behavior. No transformation or resurrection is granted here."]
	quest.544DB1000000000A.title: "The Dracolich"
	quest.544DB1000000000A.quest_desc: ["The intended Dracolich combines one Dragon Survival form with exactly one lich source, not both. Dragon growth and the chosen native resurrection anchor should be retained. The integration is experimental; confirm current build support before attempting it. This guide cannot change species or create an anchor."]
	quest.544DB1000000000B.title: "Relics: Learn Your Relic"
	quest.544DB1000000000B.quest_desc: ["Discover Relics equipment, read its ability and condition tooltips and equip it in the appropriate Curios slot. Inspect its own progression interface before spending upgrades. Relics belongs in this chapter alongside Artifacts; this checkmark does not grant equipment or rank."]
	quest.544DB1000000000C.title: "Reliquified Artifacts"
	quest.544DB1000000000C.quest_desc: ["Reliquified Artifacts integrates Artifacts equipment with Relics-style progression, including item-specific XP, ranks and durability where supported. Inspect the actual item tooltip and progression interface; do not assume all accessories use identical triggers. This is orientation, not an automatic rank or repair."]
	quest.544DB1000000000D.title: "ProjectE Energy Converters"
	quest.544DB1000000000D.quest_desc: ["ProjectE Energy Converters bridges EMC with FE and supported energy systems. Find its conversion blocks through JEI when available; follow the actual ProjectE and Project Expansion recipe gates and check the configured conversion ratios before use. This guide grants no converter and does not bypass any gate."]
}
